# Copy this file to ".env" and replace both values with your own.
# See SETUP.md, part 1.5, for exactly where to find them.
#
# Supabase dashboard -> Settings -> API Keys  (or the "Connect" button up top)
#
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL        the Project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijk.supabase.co
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   the "Publishable key" (sb_publishable_...).
#                            Older projects call this "anon public" and it is a
#                            long eyJ... string instead. Either one works.
#
# Both of these are meant to be public - they are embedded in the website and
# anyone can read them. They grant nothing on their own: every request is
# checked against the Row Level Security policies in supabase/schema.sql.
#
# NEVER put the "secret key" / "service_role" key here. That one bypasses
# every privacy rule in this app.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://yourproject.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-key
